Neon spaces (M2), part 2 of 5: window controller.

One SpacesWindowController per normal window of a regular profile, created
by SpacesWindowManager as the window is created. The visible space is the
space of the active tab, and a tab's space is derived from its container, so
nothing is stored and session restore brings both back. The controller
switches space (most recently active tab of the space, or a new tab page),
picks the container of new tabs without a source page (the visible space's,
or for a new window the last active window's), leaves a new tab page in a
space whose last tab closes while other spaces have tabs, and keeps each
space's tabs together within the pinned and unpinned tabs. space_tab_filter.h
is the small hooks target the Chromium hooks in the next patches call.
Neon code, GPL-3.0.

